Discipline and Performance Management

Master the legal procedures, practical processes & common pitfalls in manag=
ing employee discipline, misconduct & termination matters.

=20

27 & 28 August 2026

9.00am - 5.00pm | GMT +8

Concorde Hotel, Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia

Zoom Video Conference

=20

WORKSHOP OVERVIEW

This practical 2-day workshop will help participants effectively manage pro=
bationers, poor performers and employee misconduct in accordance with Malay=
sian employment and industrial relations practices. Participants will gain =
a better understanding of disciplinary procedures, performance management a=
nd termination processes to ensure fair, consistent and legally compliant w=
orkplace practices. Through case studies, discussions and practical example=
s, participants will also learn how to avoid common legal and procedural mi=
stakes that may lead to costly disputes or Industrial Court claims. The pro=
gram equips managers and HR practitioners with practical tools to maintain =
workplace discipline, improve productivity and foster better industrial har=
mony.

This 2 days interactive program will enable participants to have a better u=
nderstanding and hands-on experience of managing difficult employees, handl=
ing disciplinary and termination procedures in order to achieve better indu=
strial harmony and greater productivity.

=20

COURSE OUTLINE

DAY ONE

Session 1: Introduction

Session 2: Managing Probationers

Session 3: Managing Performance of Confirmed Employees

DAY TWO

Session 4: Managing Misconducts

Session 5: Disciplinary Process

Session 6: Post Termination Process

=20

INQUIRE/REGISTER:

Reply with =93PDF-Discipline=94 on the email subject.

=20

=20

=20

If you prefer not to receive any further emails, kindly reply and put =93re=
move-me=94 on the subject. Thank you.


